    "Only the message entry consumes host work; frame detours removed; Patch API permits only three 1.0.4 judgment sites, two 1.0.24 post-initialization drawing sites, one 1.0.10 C4 load, two 1.0.20 sidebar CALLs; 1.0.21 removes all five player-selection CALL permissions",
    "Recycled host PID cannot reuse a dead retained controller process handle",
    "Host builds reject including the Runtime execution client",
    "Partial rebuilds invalidate old verification markers; Windows build verifies PE outputs before success"
  ],
  "permitted_exceptions": [
    "1.0.21 disables every player-control capability at host and Runtime and removes five selection CALL sites; normal automation remains own-only. C4 Beta adds one execution flag-load site (explicit multiplayer risk opt-in). Two other experimental judgment features use three sites; render display uses exactly ShroudDraw/FogDraw post-initialization sites; defaults off. Render display and native aircraft waypoints are ordinary UI controls; network aircraft paths now use the ordinary event gateway without either aircraft patch; native aircraft patches are SP-only. All writes owned by the entry manager, callbacks acquire a bound-thread Capture lease. Explicit host polling feeds Runtime. Optional compatible ground-click suppression uses the existing common message boundary only, default off; no OutList rewriting",
    "Read-only game-side validation/resource reads under Runtime execution",
    "Watchdog stop/dead-host restoration only",
    "Central transport supports verified construct/enqueue and original high-level backends",
    "Local UI refresh fields/selection/cursor use guarded Runtime calls; not every operation is a network event"
